    eraseOnMovablePieceClick?: boolean;
```

Match the project's comment style (// line comments). Keep it simple:

```ts
    // Clicking an empty square or immovable piece will clear the drawing, unless this property is false.
    // When false, no click will clear the drawing.
    eraseOnClick?: boolean;
```

Hmm, simpler is better. Write it like this:

```ts
    // Whether a click on the board (empty square, non-movable piece, or movable piece) clears the drawing.
    // When false, clicking never clears the drawing.
    eraseOnClick?: boolean;
```

Keep the existing eraseOnMovablePieceClick comment mostly as-is, adjusting "regardless":

Current state: "Clicking an empty square or immovable piece will clear the drawing regardless, but when this property is true, clicking on a (currently unselected) movable piece will also clear the drawing."

Change to the following:

```ts
    // Whether a click on the board can clear the drawing; when false, no click clears it.
