Now config.ts — add the option with a comment. Current text:

```ts
  drawable?: {
    enabled?: boolean; // can draw
    visible?: boolean; // can view
    defaultSnapToValidMove?: boolean;
    // Clicking an empty square or immovable piece will clear the drawing regardless, but when this property is true,
    // clicking on a (currently unselected) movable piece will also clear the drawing.
    eraseOnMovablePieceClick?: boolean;
```

The existing comment says "regardless," but this is no longer correct. Add an `eraseOnClick` option with a comment explaining that it can be disabled. Restructuring proposal:

```ts
    // Whether clicking on an empty square, an opponent piece, or (see eraseOnMovablePieceClick) a movable piece
    // clears the drawing. Set to false to disable erase-on-click entirely.
    eraseOnClick?: boolean;
    // Clicking an empty square or immovable piece will clear the drawing, but when this property is true,
    // clicking on a (currently unselected) movable piece will also clear the drawing.
    eraseOnMovablePieceClick?: boolean;
```

Match the project's comment style (// line comments). Keep it simple:

```ts
    // Clicking an empty square or immovable piece will clear the drawing, unless this property is false.
    // When false, no click will clear the drawing.
    eraseOnClick?: boolean;
```

Hmm, simpler is better. Write it like this:

```ts
    // Whether a click on the board (empty square, non-movable piece, or movable piece) clears the drawing.
    // When false, clicking never clears the drawing.
    eraseOnClick?: boolean;
```

Keep the existing eraseOnMovablePieceClick comment mostly as-is, adjusting "regardless":

Current state: "Clicking an empty square or immovable piece will clear the drawing regardless, but when this property is true, clicking on a (currently unselected) movable piece will also clear the drawing."

Change to the following:

```ts
    // Whether a click on the board can clear the drawing; when false, no click clears it.
    eraseOnClick?: boolean;
    // Clicking an empty square or immovable piece will clear the drawing, but when this property is true,
    // clicking on a (currently unselected) movable piece will also clear the drawing.
    eraseOnMovablePieceClick?: boolean;
```

Placement: put eraseOnClick before eraseOnMovablePieceClick (master first).

